Vita: bound desktop heap reserves to the handheld process. Game data, actors,
scripts and progression are unchanged. The 64 MiB MEM1/16 MiB ARAM reserves
are enforced by the Vita Aurora adapter. Keep twice-retail archive/J2D sizes,
reserve 12 MiB system and six-times-retail game heap rather than the PC's
32 MiB system and twenty-times-retail game heap. These are initial capacities,
not a claim of a validated full-game memory budget.
The initial four-times game heap (17.2 MiB) demonstrably exhausted while loading
R_SP01 room4 after Alink ShieldArcHeap (0x7d310 requested, 0x4acf0 free).
The retail physical-address check that removes 24 MiB must not run on relocated
Vita pointers: the executable lives outside this separately allocated arena.

--- a/src/m_Do/m_Do_machine.cpp
+++ b/src/m_Do/m_Do_machine.cpp
@@ -768,7 +768,7 @@
     #endif
     JFWSystem::setMaxStdHeap(1);
 
-    #if !DEBUG
+    #if !DEBUG && !TARGET_VITA
     uintptr_t arenaHi = (uintptr_t)OSGetArenaHi();
     uintptr_t arenaLo = (uintptr_t)OSGetArenaLo();
 
@@ -855,14 +855,22 @@
 
 #if TARGET_PC
     // Change heap sizes to account for 64bit pointers & extra memory available.
+#if TARGET_VITA
+    arenaSize = 12 * 1024 * 1024;
+#else
     arenaSize = 32 * 1024 * 1024;
+#endif
     commandHeapSize *= 2;
 #if DEBUG
     dynamicLinkHeapSize *= 2;
 #endif
     archiveHeapSize *= 2;
     j2dHeapSize *= 2;
+#if TARGET_VITA
+    gameHeapSize *= 6;
+#else
     gameHeapSize *= 20; // NOTE: increased from 2 to 20 to try to solve heap alloc crashes. maybe do a better fix later
+#endif
 #endif
 
     JFWSystem::setSysHeapSize(arenaSize);
